        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Beam steering\n\nTwo coherent lanes, aimed by what they hear.\n\n**Array** holds them as one instrument. `tuning` is `together`, which both nodes here require: they compare phase between lanes, so the lanes must sit on the same frequency.\n\n**Direction finder** says where the signal is. **Beamformer** points at it: the `steer` wire carries the DF's live bearing, and `mode` is `das`, one of the modes that actually uses it. The default `mrc` ignores the bearing and just maximises signal to noise, so the wire would be drawn and do nothing.\n\nTo null an interferer instead of pointing at a signal, set `nulls_deg`, or switch `mode` to `canceller`.\n\nThe beam leaves as one clean lane, so a **Channel** decodes it exactly as it would a plain radio.\n\nFor joining lanes into a wider band instead, see the Stitch wide example: it needs `spread` tuning, which these nodes refuse."
          },
          "position": {
